  { number := 225, text := "### 4.6 Spec markdown and Lean" },
  { number := 226, text := "" },
  { number := 227, text := "1. Numbered markdown is the contract that humans read." },
  { number := 228, text := "2. Lean is a separate model of selected clauses." },
  { number := 229, text := "3. Meaning proofs SHALL NOT be treated as a second markdown form checker." },
  { number := 230, text := "" },
  { number := 231, text := "### 4.7 No invented conforming product" },
  { number := 232, text := "" },
  { number := 233, text := "1. Authors SHALL NOT claim that a conforming product exists unless the repository operator has said that product exists." },
  { number := 234, text := "" },
  { number := 235, text := "### 4.8 RFC 2119 is not replaced" },
  { number := 236, text := "" },
  { number := 237, text := "1. CATE SHALL NOT replace RFC 2119." },
  { number := 238, text := "2. Requirement keywords remain as in `0000_spec.md` Clause 4 and RFC 2119." },
  { number := 239, text := "" },
  { number := 240, text := "### 4.9 Independent work streams as parallel subagents" },
  { number := 241, text := "" },
  { number := 242, text := "1. Independent work streams SHALL run as parallel subagents." },
  { number := 243, text := "2. Authors SHALL NOT serialize two jobs that do not share a write set." },
  { number := 244, text := "3. When two specifications must land in one effort, spawn one subagent per specification on disjoint files, then one pass on shared files (registry, README, `AGENTS.md`, residual, flake)." },
  { number := 245, text := "" },
  { number := 246, text := "### 4.10 Self improvement of the encode process" },
  { number := 247, text := "" },
  { number := 248, text := "1. When friction appears in the same encode effort (hyphen leftovers, incomplete questions, README wording that does not match the registry), authors SHALL improve the encode process in that same effort." },
  { number := 249, text := "2. Authors SHALL prove that improvement with a Lean check or a skill step, not a chat reminder." },
  { number := 250, text := "" },
  { number := 251, text := "### 4.11 Size reports and git status" },
  { number := 252, text := "" },
  { number := 253, text := "1. When the operator asked for size, authors SHALL run `scc --exclude-dir ref,.git,result,lean/.lake,.direnv --exclude-ext pdf .` before and after, including the COCOMO block." },
  { number := 254, text := "2. COCOMO is fun and is not a real cost or schedule. Authors SHALL NOT pass `--no-cocomo`." },
  { number := 255, text := "3. When the operator asked for git status, authors SHALL run `git status --short`." },
  { number := 256, text := "4. Authors SHALL NOT run `git add` or `git commit` unless the operator explicitly asked for that git work." },
  { number := 257, text := "5. Git remains forbidden in this repository unless the operator explicitly asked for that git work." },
  { number := 258, text := "" },
  { number := 259, text := "### 4.12 This specification is the map" },
  { number := 260, text := "" },
  { number := 261, text := "1. This file is the catalog of domain words the spelling list allows." },
  { number := 262, text := "2. Other numbered specifications in this repository SHALL use these tokens as defined here when they use those words." },
  { number := 263, text := "3. Authors SHALL NOT treat root `VOCABULARY.md` as the catalog." },
  { number := 264, text := "4. Definitions after entry headings remain human prose for meaning beyond the isomorphism. The isomorphism does not prove that those definitions match every use in other specifications." },
  { number := 265, text := "" },
  { number := 266, text := "### 4.13 Headings the checker parses" },
  { number := 267, text := "" },
  { number := 268, text := "1. The Lean checker MUST parse each entry heading with this regular expression. A wrapping mark is written as hex 60 so this file can show the pattern without a raw wrapping mark ending a fence." },
  { number := 269, text := "" },
  { number := 270, text := "````text" },
  { number := 271, text := "^### ([A-Z])_([0-9]+) \\x60([^`]+)\\x60$" },
  { number := 272, text := "````" },
  { number := 273, text := "" },
  { number := 274, text := "2. That pattern is a heading with three hash marks, then a space, then an uppercase letter, an underscore, a positive decimal index, a space, a wrapping mark, the aspell token, and a closing wrapping mark, and nothing else on the line. An example that matches is the heading for entry A_1 whose token is ABI." },
  { number := 275, text := "3. Entry headings live outside fenced code." },
  { number := 276, text := "4. Letter section headings SHALL be exactly two hash marks, a space, and one uppercase letter, and nothing else on the line, for each letter that has entries." },
  { number := 277, text := "" },
  { number := 278, text := "### 4.14 Adding a token" },
  { number := 279, text := "" },
  { number := 280, text := "1. This specification evolves." },
  { number := 281, text := "2. Adding a word under letter L inserts it in that letter's sort and renumbers that letter so ids stay `L_1` through `L_k` with no gaps." },
  { number := 282, text := "3. Authors SHALL add the token to `aspell_words.txt`, add the heading the checker parses, and add a definition in the same effort." },
  { number := 283, text := "4. Authors SHALL keep the Lean isomorphism green." },
  { number := 284, text := "" },
  { number := 285, text := "### 4.15 Sort and uniqueness" },
  { number := 286, text := "" },
  { number := 287, text := "1. Words under a letter SHALL be sorted by ASCII without regard to case, then by ASCII code when the folded forms tie." },
  { number := 288, text := "2. Each token SHALL have exactly one `L_n` id." },
  { number := 289, text := "3. Duplicate ids and duplicate words do not conform." },
  { number := 290, text := "" },
  { number := 291, text := "### 4.16 Collisions stay tagged" },
  { number := 292, text := "" },
  { number := 293, text := "1. Systems Lean is the language. Slake is the compiler. The Lake package id `SystemsLean` is not a second language name. Those three SHALL NOT be mashed into one fact." },
  { number := 294, text := "2. Remaining work written on disk is not the Systems Lean named freestanding blocker and is not a product claim that a freestanding release has no managed Lean leftover." },
  { number := 295, text := "3. Multiplicity omega in Systems Lean prose is an ASCII word. The companion Lean constructor for that multiplicity is `unrestricted`. Those two SHALL NOT be mashed into one name." },
  { number := 296, text := "4. Leftover unstack is specified by this document. RSI does not replace that repair." },
  { number := 297, text := "5. Companion Lean collision tags in `lean/Vocabulary.lean` SHALL stay as those distinct types." },
  { number := 298, text := "" },
  { number := 299, text := "### 4.17 Lean encodings and proofs" },
  { number := 300, text := "" },
  { number := 301, text := "1. The catalog SHALL also be encoded in Lean as declarations of what must be true (structures, inductive types, and propositions)." },
  { number := 302, text := "2. For the catalog the spec encoding module is `lean/VocabularySpec.lean`. That module SHALL mark itself as a spec encoding and SHALL NOT mark itself as a proof." },
  { number := 303, text := "3. Proofs SHALL live in `lean/VocabularyProofs.lean`. That module SHALL import the spec encoding module." },
  { number := 304, text := "4. `toAspell` and `ofAspell` SHALL be inverses on well formed lists, as proved in that proof module." },
  { number := 305, text := "5. Runtime isomorphism SHALL read `0005_CATE.md` and `aspell_words.txt`." },
  { number := 306, text := "6. Lean proofs SHALL NOT be treated as the specification." },
  { number := 307, text := "7. Numbered markdown SHALL NOT be treated as a substitute for those encodings." },
  { number := 308, text := "8. Mixing spec encoding declarations and their proofs in one mash that hides the split is nonconforming in this specifications repository as specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`." },
  { number := 309, text := "" },
  { number := 310, text := "### 4.18 Sibling line encodings" },
  { number := 311, text := "" },
  { number := 312, text := "1. This file SHALL have a sibling Lean spec encoding `Spec_0005.lean` at this repository root whose physical lines match this markdown, as specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`." },
  { number := 313, text := "2. Proofs of that encoding SHALL live in `lean/Proofs_0005.lean`." },
  { number := 314, text := "3. Mixing those encodings with their proofs in one file is nonconforming." },
  { number := 315, text := "4. The Lean program `line_encodings_check` SHALL fail when a markdown line has no encoding or an encoding has no matching markdown line. It SHALL fail when compiled `encodedLines` contain leftover unstack phrases in prose outside fenced code and outside inline code, and when comments in `lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean` and `lean/VocabularySpec.lean` contain those leftover phrases. That leftover unstack check uses `Cate.leftoverUnstackPhrases` and the same scan as `spec_check`. It is a floor, not a complete English checker." },
  { number := 316, text := "" },
  { number := 317, text := "### 4.19 Product honesty" },
  { number := 318, text := "" },
  { number := 319, text := "1. beastdb work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that beastdb never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 320, text := "2. SSSSS work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that SSSSS never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 321, text := "3. Slake work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that Slake never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 322, text := "4. Continuous Integration work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that Continuous Integration never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 323, text := "5. This specification does not claim a conforming Vocabulary product exists beyond the catalog, encodings, and proofs named here." },
  { number := 324, text := "" },
  { number := 325, text := "### 4.20 Unspecified products" },
  { number := 326, text := "" },
  { number := 327, text := "1. fargo is unspecified. fargo has no numbered specification and no assigned number. Authors SHALL NOT invent a numbered specification file for fargo in this effort." },
  { number := 328, text := "2. SSSP is unspecified. SSSP has no numbered specification file and no assigned number." },
  { number := 329, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is unspecified. Carbonado has no numbered specification file and no assigned number." },
  { number := 330, text := "4. Lean Machine is unspecified. Lean Machine has no numbered specification file and no assigned number." },
  { number := 331, text := "5. Number 0009 is withdrawn. Authors SHALL NOT assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. Authors SHALL NOT treat 0009 as a published specification." },
  { number := 332, text := "6. A numbered specification file at the repository root whose number is 0009 MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if such a file is present." },
  { number := 333, text := "" },
  { number := 334, text := "### 4.21 Named gate" },
  { number := 335, text := "" },
  { number := 336, text := "1. The named gate for this specifications repository remains the gate specified in `0007_CI.md`:" },
  { number := 337, text := "" },
  { number := 338, text := "```text" },
  { number := 339, text := "nix flake check \"path:$PWD\" --print-build-logs" },
  { number := 340, text := "```" },
  { number := 341, text := "" },
  { number := 342, text := "2. Lean 4 SHALL be used to surface logical inconsistency in the encodings and in the proofs." },
  { number := 343, text := "" },
  { number := 344, text := "### 4.22 Ambiguity floor" },
  { number := 345, text := "" },
  { number := 346, text := "1. Duplicate catalog tokens SHALL fail the isomorphism." },
  { number := 347, text := "2. Leftover unstack SHALL still fail as specified in Clause 4.4." },
  { number := 348, text := "3. A numbered specification that uses the product name beastdb with wrong capitalization SHALL fail `spec_check`." },
  { number := 349, text := "4. This floor is not a complete English ambiguity checker. Authors still SHALL write complete American English thoughts." },
  { number := 350, text := "" },
  { number := 351, text := "### 4.23 Contradiction floor" },
  { number := 352, text := "" },
  { number := 353, text := "1. Registry numbers SHALL be unique." },
  { number := 354, text := "2. Registry file names SHALL be unique." },
  { number := 355, text := "3. Mixing spec encodings with their proofs in a mash that hides the split SHALL be treated as `False`." },
  { number := 356, text := "4. This floor is not a checker of every sentence pair in this repository." },
  { number := 357, text := "" },
  { number := 358, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 359, text := "" },
  { number := 360, text := "A numbered specification document conforms to this specification if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 361, text := "" },
  { number := 362, text := "1. It uses complete American English thoughts and does not use half labels as sentences (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 363, text := "2. Every question to a human names the file or clause, quotes the current wording, says why the choice matters, names the options, uses ordinary English, defines a new phrase in the same sentence when one is introduced, and says what we will do for each option (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 364, text := "3. Prose is concise, names the real thing, and does not use decoder ring jargon (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 365, text := "4. Hyphenated compounds of the kind used in legal captions are rephrased; leftover unstack is absent from numbered specification prose outside fenced code and inline code; `high assurance`, `3 bit`, and `time series` are not treated as leftover unstack merely for having a space (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 366, text := "5. Residual is written in full on disk when the document names unpublished specifications, unassigned numbers, unpinned prior art, unimplemented requirements, or out of scope items; a numbered specification other than 0000 that contains a planned or unpublished `NNNN_*.md` token includes a Residual heading (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 367, text := "6. Numbered markdown is treated as the contract humans read, and Lean meaning proofs are not treated as a second markdown form checker (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 368, text := "7. It does not claim that a conforming product exists unless the repository operator has said that product exists (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 369, text := "8. It does not replace RFC 2119 or invent a private mapping that weakens RFC 2119 keywords (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 370, text := "" },
  { number := 371, text := "An encode effort in this repository conforms to this specification if and only if all of the following hold, in addition to items 1 through 8 of this clause as they apply to the effort:" },
  { number := 372, text := "" },
  { number := 373, text := "1. Independent work streams run as parallel subagents on disjoint write sets (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 374, text := "2. Friction in the same encode effort improves the encode process, proved with a Lean check or a skill step (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 375, text := "3. Size reports include COCOMO when the operator asked for size, and git status is `git status --short` when the operator asked for git status, without `git add` or `git commit` unless the operator asked (Clause 4.11)." },
  { number := 376, text := "" },
  { number := 377, text := "Work that claims the catalog in this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 378, text := "" },
  { number := 379, text := "1. This file is the catalog; other numbered specifications use these tokens as defined here when they use those words; root `VOCABULARY.md` is a pointer and is not the catalog (Clause 4.12)." },
  { number := 380, text := "2. Entry headings match the heading pattern the checker parses; letter headings are one uppercase letter (Clause 4.13)." },
  { number := 381, text := "3. Adding a token updates the spelling list, the heading, the definition, and ids for that letter, and the Lean isomorphism stays green (Clause 4.14)." },
  { number := 382, text := "4. Tokens are unique and sorted as specified (Clause 4.15)." },
  { number := 383, text := "5. Collision tags stay distinct as specified (Clause 4.16)." },
  { number := 384, text := "6. Spec encodings live in `lean/VocabularySpec.lean`; proofs live in `lean/VocabularyProofs.lean`; runtime isomorphism reads this file; a mash of encodings and proofs is treated as nonconforming (Clause 4.17)." },
  { number := 385, text := "7. Sibling `Spec_0005.lean` matches this markdown; proofs live in `lean/Proofs_0005.lean`; `line_encodings_check` fails on drift and on leftover unstack in compiled encodings and in named spec encoding comments (Clause 4.18)." },
  { number := 386, text := "8. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are treated as ongoing and not ready for use, and are not described as never started or as ready (Clause 4.19)." },
  { number := 387, text := "9. fargo, SSSP, Carbonado, and Lean Machine remain unspecified; number 0009 is withdrawn and is not assigned to fargo or Carbonado; a numbered specification file for 0009 does not exist (Clause 4.20)." },
  { number := 388, text := "10. The named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate for this repository (Clause 4.21)." },
  { number := 389, text := "11. Duplicate catalog tokens fail the isomorphism; leftover unstack still fails; this is not a complete English ambiguity checker (Clause 4.22)." },
  { number := 390, text := "12. Registry numbers and file names are unique; a mash of encodings and proofs is `False`; this is not a checker of every sentence pair (Clause 4.23)." },
  { number := 391, text := "" },
  { number := 392, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming implementation of a product. Meeting these items is a claim about a document or an encode effort, not about this markdown file as a shipped engine." },
  { number := 393, text := "" },
  { number := 394, text := "Optional recommendations (SHOULD, RECOMMENDED) do not break conformance when unmet, but authors SHOULD follow them unless there is a clear reason not to." },
  { number := 395, text := "" },
  { number := 396, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 397, text := "" },
  { number := 398, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, unpinned prior art, or an unimplemented requirement named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 399, text := "" },
  { number := 400, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 401, text := "" },
  { number := 402, text := "1. fargo has no assigned specification number. A previous plan that assigned number 0005 to fargo is withdrawn. Number 0005 is this specification (CATE). Number 0006 is Recursive Self Improvement (`0006_RSI.md`). This document does not invent a new number for fargo." },
  { number := 403, text := "2. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Discussion has mentioned 0006 as a possible later number for Carbonado. That mention is not an assignment. Number 0005 is this specification (CATE). Number 0006 is Recursive Self Improvement. This document does not create a Carbonado numbered file." },
  { number := 404, text := "3. Number 0009 is withdrawn. The word catalog is this specification. A numbered specification file for 0009 MUST NOT exist. Number 0009 is not fargo and is not Carbonado. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, or 0010 for fargo or for Carbonado." },
  { number := 405, text := "4. The Surmount Systems System Prompt (SSSP) is not specified. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 406, text := "5. Lean Machine is named as a substrate in `0002_Systems_Lean.md` and in `0004_SSSSS.md`. It has no numbered specification and no assigned number. This document does not invent a numbered file for Lean Machine." },
  { number := 407, text := "" },
  { number := 408, text := "### 6.2 Unpinned prior art" },
  { number := 409, text := "" },
  { number := 410, text := "1. ISO 24495-1:2023 and the US Federal Plain Language Guidelines are informative prior art named in Clause 2.2. They are not under this repository's `ref/`. They are not Clause 12 Form 1 or Form 2 pins. This document does not add those pins." },
  { number := 411, text := "2. Formal Vibefication essays are cited by URL. They are not Clause 12 pins. This repository does not vendor those essays as Form 2 copies under `ref/`. Full license text is still not published on `https://proofofkeags.com` . Do not invent that license." },
  { number := 412, text := "" },
  { number := 413, text := "### 6.3 Mechanical floor, not a complete English checker" },
  { number := 414, text := "" },
  { number := 415, text := "1. The leftover unstack list in Clause 3.5 is a floor, not a complete English checker. Complete sentence quality is not fully mechanical. `spec_check` flags the listed leftover phrases in numbered specification prose and requires a Residual heading when a numbered specification other than 0000 contains a planned file token. `line_encodings_check` flags those leftover phrases in compiled sibling `encodedLines` (outside fenced code and inline code) and in comments of `lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean` and `lean/VocabularySpec.lean`, using `Cate.leftoverUnstackPhrases` and the same leftover unstack scan as `spec_check`. It does not prove that every sentence is complete, and it does not claim that every Lean comment is a complete American English thought." },
  { number := 416, text := "2. Duplicate catalog tokens fail the isomorphism (Clause 4.15 and Clause 4.22). That check is not a complete English ambiguity checker. This document does not claim to resolve every ambiguous English sentence." },
  { number := 417, text := "" },
  { number := 418, text := "### 6.4 Contradiction floor, not every sentence pair" },
  { number := 419, text := "" },
  { number := 420, text := "1. Registry numbers and file names are unique. Mixing spec encodings with their proofs in a mash that hides the split is `False` (Clause 4.23)." },
  { number := 421, text := "2. That floor is not a checker of every pair of sentences in this repository. This document does not claim to detect every contradiction in prose." },
  { number := 422, text := "" },
  { number := 423, text := "### 6.5 Agent conformance is not claimed" },
  { number := 424, text := "" },
  { number := 425, text := "1. This document specifies CATE for numbered specifications and for agents that encode them. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that every agent already conforms." },
  { number := 426, text := "2. This document does not claim that a conforming product exists." },
  { number := 427, text := "3. Continuous Integration is specified in `0007_CI.md`. Number 0007 is not CATE. This document does not replace that specification." },
  { number := 428, text := "" },
  { number := 429, text := "### 6.6 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 430, text := "" },
  { number := 431, text := "1. The products named here are ongoing and are not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 432, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product as specified in `0007_CI.md`. This document does not claim that match already holds." },
  { number := 433, text := "3. The SSSSS and beastdb reality check named in `0007_CI.md` is a requirement on that stack. SSSSS and beastdb are ongoing and not ready for use. Do not write that they never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 434, text := "" },
  { number := 435, text := "### 6.7 Definitions remain human prose" },
  { number := 436, text := "" },
  { number := 437, text := "1. Entry definitions in this file remain human prose for meaning beyond the isomorphism of tokens and ids." },
  { number := 438, text := "2. The Lean isomorphism does not prove that those definitions are complete, and it does not prove that every use in another numbered specification already matches the prose here." },
  { number := 439, text := "3. Filling or revising those definitions is remaining work as the catalog evolves." },
  { number := 440, text := "" },
  { number := 441, text := "### 6.8 Other meaning models still mix encodings and proofs" },
  { number := 442, text := "" },
  { number := 443, text := "1. This specification follows the Formal Vibefication split for `lean/VocabularySpec.lean` and `lean/VocabularyProofs.lean`, and for `Spec_0005.lean` and `lean/Proofs_0005.lean`." },
  { number := 444, text := "2. Companion models for CATE meaning, RSI, Continuous Integration, beastdb, SSSSS, and Systems Lean still place theorems in the same Lean module as the encodings they prove. That mash is remaining work under `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. It is not a claim that mash conforms." },
  { number := 445, text := "3. Collision tags in `lean/Vocabulary.lean` still mix encodings and proofs. That mash is remaining work under 0008." },
  { number := 446, text := "" },
  { number := 447, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 448, text := "" },
  { number := 449, text := "### 1.1.0 - 20260825" },
  { number := 450, text := "" },
  { number := 451, text := "Renumbers this specification to 0005 with file name `0005_CATE.md`. Recursive Self Improvement is specified in `0006_RSI.md`. CATE is not specification 0006. Adds that a question to a human uses ordinary English, defines a new phrase in the same sentence when one is introduced, and says what we will do for each option." },
  { number := 452, text := "" },
  { number := 453, text := "This 1.1.0 also folds the Vocabulary catalog (formerly numbered specification 0009) into this specification. Number 0009 is withdrawn. Root `VOCABULARY.md` remains a short pointer to this file. Runtime isomorphism reads this file, not the pointer." },
  { number := 454, text := "" },
  { number := 455, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260825" },
  { number := 456, text := "" },
  { number := 457, text := "First publication of Concise American Technical English as a numbered specification. Moves CATE out of `0000_spec.md` Clause 20 into this document. `0000_spec.md` version 1.2.0 keeps a short pointer only and does not restate CATE. Authors still SHALL apply CATE by following this specification. That 1.0.0 assigned this document number 0006; version 1.1.0 corrects the stack number to 0005." },
  { number := 458, text := "" },
  { number := 459, text := "This 1.0.0 states complete American English thoughts, questions to humans that name file or clause, current wording, why it matters, and options, concise prose, leftover unstack as nonconforming with the floor list in Clause 3.5, residual written in full, numbered markdown as the contract humans read, no invented conforming product, CATE as not a replacement for RFC 2119, independent work streams as parallel subagents, self improvement of the encode process in the same effort proved with a Lean check or a skill step, and size reports that include COCOMO when the operator asked for size." },
  { number := 460, text := "" },
  { number := 461, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: fargo has no assigned specification number; Carbonado has no assigned number; ISO 24495-1:2023 and the US Federal Plain Language Guidelines are informative prior art and are not Clause 12 pins; this document does not claim that every agent already conforms." },
  { number := 462, text := "" },
  { number := 463, text := "No prior public release of this specification as a numbered document exists. CATE text in `0000_spec.md` 1.1.0 was not a numbered specification." },
